(Shows the PowerShell script execution policy for various scopes, e.g., user, computer, process. That is, it checks the current security settings for scripts)

Get-ExecutionPolicy -List

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Sets the policy for the entire computer.

Set-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope LocalMachine

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Shows the last 20 events from the PowerShell log. There you can see, e.g., executed commands, errors, PowerShell activity)

Get-WinEvent -LogName "Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational" -MaxEvents 20

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(causes Windows to record PowerShell activity in this log)

wevtutil sl Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational /e:true

